title: Famine on the Volga
subtitle: Soviet Russia is starving, and asks the workers of the world for bread.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1921 and month >= 9 and month <= 10 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 5
on-arrival: soviet_russia_status = 'Famine on the Volga; the New Economic Policy'

= Famine on the Volga

After drought and seven years of war, famine has struck the Volga. Millions are starving. Lenin has accepted help even from Herbert Hoover's American Relief Administration.

In Berlin, Willi Münzenberg has founded the Workers' International Relief to collect money, food and tools for Soviet Russia. He wants the party behind it and not in front of it, so that anyone who wants to help can.

- @broad: Collect with the unions and the SPD.
- @party: Run the collection through the party's own offices.

@broad
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The relief gets the credit, not the party. Lenin will like it.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids joint campaigns with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 3;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
RG.ecci('lenin', 4);
!}

Collection committees form in factories where communists and social democrats have not spoken for two years. Lorries leave Berlin for Petrograd with flour, medicine and tractors.

@party
subtitle: Brings in 2 funds, for the organisation's costs. Münzenberg will protest.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += 2;
Q.worker_support -= 2;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', 3);
!}

The party runs the collection through its own offices and keeps a share for the organisation's costs. Münzenberg protests and is overruled. The *Vorwärts* asks how much of the flour reached the Volga.
